pages={
'/about/':('About & Contact | Sleep Reset System','Learn about the purpose and limits of Sleep Reset System and find product support.','''<h1>A practical place to start.</h1><p>Sleep Reset System is an independent educational resource for adults who want to explore more consistent sleep habits. The guide organises general sleep education, routine ideas and a sleep diary into a 21-day framework.</p><h2>Who created this?</h2><p>The guide is published under the Sleep Reset System name. Its creator is not a doctor, sleep specialist, licensed therapist or medical organisation. The resource draws on publicly available sleep information and does not offer personalised healthcare.</p><h2>Questions and support</h2><p>For questions before buying, seller contact information, delivery help or refund enquiries, visit the <a href="https://payhip.com/b/xZzcv">product listing on Payhip</a> and use the seller contact option provided there. If you have purchased, also refer to your receipt.</p><h2>Editorial approach</h2><p>We describe the guide's contents without promising a medical outcome. Free educational content links to public health sources where relevant. The website and PDF do not replace assessment from a qualified healthcare professional.</p>'''),
'/privacy/':('Privacy | Sleep Reset System','How this website handles privacy and links to Payhip.','''<h1>Privacy notice</h1><p>Last updated: 30 October 2026.</p><p>This static website does not include an account system, contact form, advertising pixels or analytics scripts. We do not ask you to submit health information here.</p><h2>Technical information</h2><p>The hosting and network providers may process technical request data, such as IP addresses, browser information and access logs, to deliver and secure the website. Their processing is governed by their own terms and privacy notices.</p><h2>Purchases on Payhip</h2><p>Purchase links take you to Payhip. Payhip and its payment providers process information needed for checkout and delivery under their own policies. Read <a href="https://payhip.com/privacy">Payhip’s privacy policy</a> before purchasing. This website does not receive your payment card details.</p><h2>Cookies and future changes</h2><p>The website code does not set cookies or use browser storage. Hosting providers may use security mechanisms. If analytics, advertising or forms are added, this notice and any required consent controls should be updated before those features are enabled.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For product or privacy questions, use the seller contact option on the <a href="https://payhip.com/b/xZzcv">Payhip listing</a>.</p>'''),
'/terms/':('Terms & Purchases | Sleep Reset System','Understand the educational scope of the guide and where to review purchase details.','''<h1>Terms & purchase information</h1><p>Last updated: 30 October 2026.</p><h2>Educational use</h2><p>This website and the guide provide general information for adults. They do not diagnose, treat, cure or prevent medical or psychiatric conditions. They are not a substitute for personalised medical advice, clinician-delivered CBT-I, therapy or medication.</p><h2>Digital product and checkout</h2><p>Sleep Reset System is a digital PDF, not a physical item. Purchases take place on <a href="https://payhip.com/b/xZzcv">Payhip</a>. Check the current price, currency, applicable taxes, delivery information and seller terms there before purchasing.</p><h2>Refund enquiries</h2><p>Review the seller’s refund terms on Payhip before paying. For refund or delivery questions, contact the seller using the listing or purchase receipt. Nothing here removes any consumer rights that apply to your purchase.</p><h2>No guaranteed results</h2><p>The 21-day framework is an organisational format. Results and experiences vary. No sleep improvement or clinical outcome is guaranteed.</p><h2>Copyright</h2><p>The guide is copyrighted by Sleep Reset System. Purchase does not transfer copyright or grant permission to redistribute or resell it.</p>'''),
'/sleep-habit-guide/':('How to Start a Consistent Sleep Routine | Sleep Reset System','A simple introduction to observing sleep habits, planning an evening wind-down and using a sleep diary.','''<div class="eyebrow">Read & learn · 30 October 2026</div><h1>Start with your routine, not a perfect night.</h1><p>By Sleep Reset System · General educational content</p><p>When evenings feel unpredictable, a useful first step is to look at the routine around sleep. This is an introduction to everyday habits, not a treatment plan for insomnia.</p><h2>Observe before changing everything</h2><p>Write down what your evening usually looks like: finishing work, having dinner, using screens and getting into bed. Note your wake time too. A short record can help you describe your routine more clearly without judging each night as a success or failure.</p><h2>Make room to wind down</h2><p>The US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute suggests allowing quiet time before bed, keeping a consistent schedule and making the bedroom quiet, cool and dark. Choose a manageable idea that suits your circumstances, such as reading quietly or setting work aside earlier.</p><p>These are general habits. They cannot explain every sleep problem, and they are not a replacement for healthcare.</p><h2>Use a sleep diary as a record</h2><p>A diary gives you a place to note approximate bedtimes, wake times and observations. Its purpose is to capture patterns, not to chase a perfect score. If tracking makes you more anxious, discuss that with a qualified professional.</p><h2>Know when self-help is not enough</h2><p>If sleep difficulties persist, are severe or interfere with daily life, speak with a healthcare professional. Avoid changing medication or using restrictive sleep schedules based only on online information.</p><h2>Want an organised framework?</h2><p>The <a href="/">Sleep Reset System guide</a> brings routine education, checklists and a 21-day diary into one PDF. The time frame provides structure; it does not promise a particular result.</p><a class="button" href="https://payhip.com/b/xZzcv">Explore the guide on Payhip ↗</a><h2>Further reading</h2><p><a href="https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/health/sleep-deprivation/healthy-sleep-habits">NHLBI: Healthy sleep habits</a><br><a href="https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/health/insomnia/treatment">NHLBI: Insomnia treatment and CBT-I</a></p>''')}
